// Adversarial: Tether at maximum-practical stacks (7) under sustained chaos input.
// At stack 7: damage redirect is 85% and coverage is capped at 100% -- every
// eligible adjacent pair in the Dense layout is linked. The Dense layout provides
// ~20 cells in a grid, maximising the number of tether links and the frequency
// of simultaneous bilateral redirects.
//
// Bilateral redirect stress: A is linked to B, B is linked to A. When the bolt
// hits both A and B in the same tick (e.g. pierce pass or two bolts), each hit
// emits a redirect: A's redirect targets B (85% damage), B's redirect targets A
// (85% damage). Both redirects carry source_chip = "hazard:tether" (sentinel).
// On delivery, each redirect must be skipped by the sentinel check -- if the
// check fails, B's redirect triggers another redirect back to A, and A's triggers
// one back to B, producing geometrically-growing message chains that eventually
// cause NoNaN (HP underflows NaN), NoEntityLeaks (message entity accumulation),
// or a panic from infinite recursion.
//
// At 7 stacks with 100% coverage, many cells are central nodes in multiple eligible
// pairs. The mutual-exclusion rule means each cell participates in exactly one pair,
// so there is no multi-hop chain -- but the high redirect percentage (85%) means
// the partner often takes more damage than the original target, creating cell kill
// ordering races: A takes 100 damage and lives (HP 50), B takes 85 redirect damage
// and dies (HP 0). If B's cleanup_broken_tether_links fires before A's next
// redirect delivery, A loses its TetherLink and the sentinel is never needed --
// but if the redirect is delivered before cleanup, A's link must still be valid.
// Any ordering inversion here can leave stale TetherLink components (caught
// indirectly by NoEntityLeaks via unexpected component accumulation).
//
// HazardStackValid confirms the 7 Tether stacks remain valid throughout.
// NoNaN guards against HP underflow to NaN under the 85% redirect arithmetic.
// NoEntityLeaks guards against stale message or component accumulation.
//
// Stress: 32 runs explore different RNG seeds, varying which pairs are linked
// and which cells take damage first -- maximising coverage of the mutual-exclusion
// matching and sentinel-guard paths in the redirect pipeline.
(
    breaker: "Aegis",
    layout: "Dense",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 5000,
    disallowed_failures: [BoltInBounds, BreakerCountReasonable, BreakerInBounds, HazardStackValid, NoEntityLeaks, NoNaN],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    allow_early_end: false,
    stress: (runs: 32, parallelism: 32),
    seed: 3377,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 5, mutation: InjectHazardStack(kind_name: "Tether", stacks: 7)),
    ],
)
